// Oxikube k9s base keymap (E21-S09), selected with `"base_keymap": "k9s"` in settings.json.
//
// The per-OS defaults already carry k9s's verbs (y YAML, d describe, e edit, l logs, s shell,
// a attach, ctrl-d delete, shift-f / f port forwards, ctrl-w wide, ctrl-k kill, z sanitize,
// o show node, shift-j owner, 0-9 namespaces, `:` the jump bar, `?` help). This layer holds only
// what the defaults leave out; like every base keymap it sits between the defaults and your own
// keymap.json, so your bindings still win. Only existing actions are bound.
//
//   c   copy the name of the cursor row (k9s). On the Nodes table `c` keeps meaning cordon, as in
//       k9s, so that table is excluded here.
//   q   close the detail drawer and return to the table (k9s: `q` backs out of a detail view).
[
  {
    "context": "ResourceTable && !Editing && kind != Node",
    "bindings": {
      "c": "resource_table::CopyName"
    }
  },
  {
    "context": "DetailDrawer && !Editing",
    "bindings": {
      "q": "resource_detail::Close"
    }
  }
]
